@startuml GitHub OAuth Authentication Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title GitHub OAuth 2.0 Authentication Flow - Project3

actor User as user
participant "Angular App\n(Browser)" as browser #LightBlue
participant "ASP.NET API\n(Your Server)" as backend #LightGreen
participant "GitHub OAuth\n(github.com)" as github #Orange
participant "GitHub API\n(api.github.com)" as githubapi #Orange

== Phase 1: Initiate Login ==
user -> browser: Click "Login" button
activate browser
browser -> browser: loginComponent.login()
note right
  Construct OAuth URL with:
  - client_id from environment.ts
  - redirect_uri = {origin}/login
end note
browser -> github: **Redirect** to /login/oauth/authorize\n?client_id={clientId}\n&redirect_uri={yourApp}/login
deactivate browser

== Phase 2: GitHub Authorization ==
activate github
github -> user: Display authorization page\n"Authorize Project3?"
user -> github: Click "Authorize application"
github -> github: Generate authorization code
github -> browser: **302 Redirect** to {yourApp}/login\n?code={authorizationCode}
deactivate github

== Phase 3: Exchange Authorization Code for Access Token ==
activate browser
browser -> browser: ngOnInit() detects\n'code' query parameter
note right
  LoginComponent extracts
  code from URL params
end note
browser -> backend: **POST** /api/login\n{\n  "code": "{authCode}"\n}
deactivate browser

activate backend
backend -> backend: Add client_id & client_secret\nfrom appsettings.json
note right
  Server adds sensitive credentials:
  - client_id
  - client_secret
  (Never exposed to browser)
end note
backend -> github: **POST** /login/oauth/access_token\n{\n  "code": "{authCode}",\n  "client_id": "{id}",\n  "client_secret": "{secret}"\n}
activate github
github -> github: Validate credentials\nand authorization code
github -> backend: **200 OK**\n{\n  "access_token": "{token}",\n  "token_type": "bearer",\n  "scope": "read:user"\n}
deactivate github
backend -> browser: **200 OK**\n{\n  "access_token": "{token}"\n}
deactivate backend

== Phase 4: Store Token and Fetch User Profile ==
activate browser
browser -> browser: AuthService.setToken()\nStore in sessionStorage
note right
  Token stored as:
  sessionStorage['github_token']
end note
browser -> backend: **GET** /api/login/user\nAuthorization: Bearer {token}
deactivate browser

activate backend
backend -> githubapi: **GET** /user\nAuthorization: Bearer {token}\nUser-Agent: Project3/1.0
activate githubapi
githubapi -> githubapi: Validate access token
githubapi -> backend: **200 OK**\n{\n  "login": "username",\n  "id": 12345,\n  "avatar_url": "...",\n  "name": "Full Name",\n  "email": "user@example.com"\n}
deactivate githubapi
backend -> browser: **200 OK**\n{ user data }
deactivate backend

activate browser
browser -> browser: Update authState$\n{\n  isAuthenticated: true,\n  user: { ... },\n  token: "{token}"\n}
browser -> browser: router.navigateByUrl()\nto requested page
browser -> user: Show logged-in UI\nDisplay user avatar & name
deactivate browser

note over user, githubapi
  **User is now authenticated!**
  - Token stored in sessionStorage
  - User profile cached in AuthService
  - Protected routes now accessible
end note

@enduml
